KSU side susfs patches
======================

KSU side susfs integration for forks whose sources do not ship one.
Generated against exact refs of the forks, so regenerate the patch if
their ref moves:

  mksu.patch        5ec1cff/KernelSU    @ main     (from midori official.patch)
  jingmatrix.patch  JingMatrix/KernelSU @ dev      (from midori official.patch)
  mambosu.patch     RapliVx/KernelSU    @ master   (from midori kow.patch)

How they were generated: clone the fork ref, apply the upstream patch
with `patch -p1`, hand merge the failing hunks (with the fork tree),
then `git diff` against the pristine fork. Verified with `patch -p1
--dry-run` against a fresh clone of the same ref.

mksu and mambosu deliberately drop the pkg_observer.c hunk that calls
susfs_parse_priority_app_strings(): both forks refactored throne
tracking and no longer have ksu_defer_track_throne, and nothing
upstream (SukiSU-Ultra or current midori01) calls it either, since ksud
drives the priority uid filter through its own susfs command.

FinaSU (LyraVoid/FinaSU @ master) already embeds KSU side susfs with
its own extension/susfs.c, so it needs no patch. Official, KowSU, xxKSU
and the SukiSU family carry their own integration upstream.
